    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1974-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "If \\(g(x)=\\frac{1}{2},\\) then \\(x^2=\\frac{1}{2},\\) and either corresponding \\(x\\) is nonzero. Hence \\[ f(\\frac{1}{2})=\\frac{1-x^2}{x^2} =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}}{\\frac{1}{2}}=1. \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Choose a nonzero \\(x\\) for which \\(g(x)=\\frac{1}{2}\\)",
        "The equation \\(1-x^2=\\frac{1}{2}\\) determines \\(x^2\\) directly"
      ],
